1. Executive Summary
This project analyses the Olist Brazilian e-commerce dataset to understand sales performance, customer purchasing behaviour, product-category demand, seller contribution and delivery outcomes. The analysis was performed in MySQL 8.0 using joins, aggregations, subqueries, common table expressions, window functions, a view and a stored procedure.
The results provide a historical view of the marketplace rather than a measure of current performance. The dataset ends on 17 October 2018. Revenue in this report follows a consistent rule: item price from delivered orders only; freight is shown separately.
